==== Installing OpenWrt ====
OpenWrt can be installed via the EVA bootloader. The EVA bootloader waits in the first 5 seconds after power-on for an FTP connection on 192.168.178.1.
Set your IP address to 192.168.178.2 and upload the image like following.

<code>
ftp -n -4 192.168.178.1

ftp> quote USER adam2
ftp> quote PASS adam2
ftp> binary
ftp> debug
ftp> passive
ftp> quote MEDIA FLSH
ftp> put openwrt-sysupgrade.bin mtd1
ftp> close
ftp> quit
</code>

The process can take up to 3 minutes. After a minute, the INFO LED will illuminate Red. Once the LED turns off the process is complete and you need to powercycle to boot up OpenWrt.

:!: **Linux only warning:** the above process can only be done with **Linux ftp** or e.g. **Ubuntu on Windows**. The **native ftp.exe** of Window does **not** support **passive mode** which is required by adam2 ftp.



===== Firmware =====
AVM GPL code can be found on [[https://osp.avm.de/fritzbox/fritzbox-4020/|their FTP]].

In case you are using the AVM provided recover.exe, a counter on the tffs partition will increment. It is located at 0x7AE and labeled as recovered. It currently does not seem to be incremented by the Installation methods mentioned in the next section.

==== Reverting back to stock ====
To revert back to the AVM stock-firmware, you need to download the image provided on [[https://ftp.avm.de/fritzbox/fritzbox-4020/deutschland/fritz.os/|their ftp]] (ending in .image).

Rename the downloaded file from xyz.image to xyz.tar and extract the archive. In the /var/tmp subdirectory you find a kernel.image file. Flash it like the above described process for OpenWrt installation, use the kernel.image in the last step.


===== Hardware =====
==== Info ====
^ SoC              | Qualcomm QCA9561 (Dragonfly) 720MHz       |
^ RAM              | 128MB (Winbond W971GG6KB-25)              |
^ Flash            | 16 MiB SPI-NOR (Macronix MX25L12835F)     |
^ WiFi             | Qualcomm QCA9561 3x3 b/g/n                |
^ Bootloader       | ADAM2/EVA                                 |
^ Ethernet         | 4 x 100 Mbit/s LAN / 1 x 100 Mbit/s WAN   |
^ USB              | 1x USB 2.0                                |
^ Serial console   | onboard                                   |

==== Different Antenna Layouts ====
There seem to be two different antenna layouts. One with all three antennas parallel and an other layout where two antennas are parellel and one is orthogonal. See images below:

<WRAP center round box 60%>
{{ media:avm:fritzbox_4020_orthogonal-antenna.jpg?nolink&400 |}}
Two antennas are parallel, one is orthogonal.
</WRAP>

<WRAP center round box 60%>
{{ media:avm:fritzbox_4020_parallel-antenna.jpg?nolink&400 |}}
All three antennas are parallel.
</WRAP>


==== UART ====
Serial pinout is described [[https://i.imgur.com/oeiQiUX.jpg|here]]. Don't connect to 3.3V! Set to 115200N8 for connection.

